From: Scott Haseley <shaseley@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:20:26 -0700
Subject: [scheduler] Unregister microtask callback in ~EventLoop

Since the MicrotaskQueue now lives on the Oilpan heap and is no longer
destroyed when EventLoop is destroyed, it can leave a dangling EventLoop
pointer stored with the MicrotasksCompletedCallback. This CL fixes this
by clearing the callback on event loop destruction.

Fixed: 568988525
Change-Id: I89ac2f003e298a6bbbf545c4482f26cf489a3164
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8516108
Reviewed-by: Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Scott Haseley <shaseley@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712555}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
This branch's ~EventLoop() already had a DCHECK(schedulers_.empty()) body instead of being defaulted; the callback unregistration was added after it, unchanged.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/common/event_loop.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/common/event_loop.cc
index 795d7a8dcca6d6c7d02bfa6d478f563e4b6235b6..8888ce26a41fcbba315f6a19b59b96b45297f8eb 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/common/event_loop.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/scheduler/common/event_loop.cc
@@ -55,6 +55,11 @@ EventLoop::EventLoop(Delegate* delegate,
 
 EventLoop::~EventLoop() {
   DCHECK(schedulers_.empty());
+  // `microtask_queue_` may be cleared before sweeping during heap termination.
+  if (microtask_queue_) {
+    microtask_queue_->RemoveMicrotasksCompletedCallback(
+        &EventLoop::RunEndOfCheckpointTasks, this);
+  }
 }
 
 void EventLoop::EnqueueMicrotask(base::OnceClosure task) {
